  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Engagement coastal protection Cirebon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The northern coast of Java faces growing climate risks, rapid urbanisation, and severe land subsidence, making cities like Jakarta, Cirebon, and Demak increasingly vulnerable. Coastal protection has therefore become a key priority for President Prabowo, supported by a newly established authority for integrated coastal management. Within the longstanding Indonesia&#x2013;Netherlands water partnership, several initiatives have been implemented, including National Capital Integrated Coastal Development (NCICD), Building with Nature Demak, and the Blue Deal program. Invest International Public Programmes (IIPP) is preparing investments in coastal protection for Demak and Cirebon, focusing on a &#x201c;restructuring&#x201d; approach for Demak and a &#x201c;defense&#x201d; approach for Cirebon. This assignment focuses on Cirebon and aims to identify potential intervention scenarios, assess them through expert and stakeholder input, and conduct field measurements to inform a future feasibility study. The outcomes will be consolidated into an overview and an input package for IIPP&#x2019;s Feasibility Study Phase.</narrative>
  </description>
